      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Inscribed angle",
        "body": "The octagon is inscribed in a circle, and its vertices cut the circle into $8$ equal arcs of $45^\\circ$. The angle $x$ is an inscribed angle that stands on the arc of $3$ sides ($135^\\circ$), so $x=\\frac12\\cdot135^\\circ=67\\frac12^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $67\\frac12$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Isosceles triangles",
        "body": "Each interior angle of the octagon is $135^\\circ$. At the top-right vertex $x$ sits between the two chords. The triangle formed by that vertex and the next two vertices is isosceles with apex $135^\\circ$, so its base angle there is $22\\frac12^\\circ$. The quadrilateral with three octagon sides (ending at the chord) is an isosceles trapezoid with angles $135^\\circ,135^\\circ,45^\\circ,45^\\circ$, so the angle between the side and the long chord is $45^\\circ$. Hence $x=135^\\circ-45^\\circ-22\\frac12^\\circ=67\\frac12^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $67\\frac12$**"
      }
    ],
