    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Telescoping",
        "body": "$\\frac1{k(k+1)}=\\frac1k-\\frac1{k+1}$. Start with $\\frac1{1\\times2}=\\frac12$. Then $\\frac1{2\\times3}+\\dots+\\frac1{49\\times50}=\\frac12-\\frac1{50}$. The value is $\\frac12-\\left(\\frac12-\\frac1{50}\\right)=\\frac1{50}$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $\\frac1{50}$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pattern",
        "body": "$\\frac12-\\frac16=\\frac13$, $\\frac13-\\frac1{12}=\\frac14$, $\\frac14-\\frac1{20}=\\frac15$, so after subtracting up to $\\frac1{n(n+1)}$ the value is $\\frac1{n+1}$. For $n=49$: $\\frac1{50}$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $\\frac1{50}$**"
      }
