      {
        "title": "Triangular numbers",
        "body": "Row $n$ has $n$ numbers, and the last number of row $n$ is $\\frac{n(n+1)}2$. Row $50$ ends with $\\frac{50\\cdot51}2=1275$, so row $51$ runs from $1276$ to $1326$ ($51$ numbers). The middle (26th) number is $1275+26=1301$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 1301**"
