    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the side",
        "body": "Let the hexagon have side $s$. The shaded triangle has the bottom side as base ($s$) and its apex at the midpoint of the top side, so its height is the full height of the hexagon, $\\sqrt3\\,s$. Its area is $\\frac{\\sqrt3}2s^2$. The hexagon has area $6\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}4s^2=\\frac{3\\sqrt3}2s^2$. The ratio is $\\frac13$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $\\frac13$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Six equilateral triangles",
        "body": "Split the hexagon into $6$ equilateral triangles from its centre, each of area $t$. The bottom triangle has the bottom side as base and height $h_0$ (from the centre). The shaded triangle has the same base but its apex is on the top side, which is at distance $2h_0$ from the bottom side. So its area is $2t$ and the fraction is $\\frac{2t}{6t}=\\frac13$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $\\frac13$**"
      }
